#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0503 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution (review H2): the stem rules skip a standard library variable structurally - ADT resolves to the BDS literal ADT at the first tier and reaches no stem, so var_name(\"LIBRARY\") is ADT, not *DT, and this rule is silent on it whatever its label. A mislabelled ADT is the exact-label rules' finding (CDISC-AD0708 / AD0709 compare 'Foo' with the published 'Analysis Date'), not a second report here. Until this plan AD0503 had no skip at all and fired on it too."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC ADT name=ADT label="Analysis Date"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *DT name=*DT label="{Date}"
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ADT type=Char label="Foo"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | x
---
